{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Claimed; grounding evidence gathered. (1) Inline merge confirmed at src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py lines 629-633 inside _build_snapshot (fetch_snapshot delegates there): `for snap_key, links in issuelinks_map.items(): if snap_key in snapshot and isinstance(links, list): snapshot[snap_key]['issuelinks'] = links`. (2) The hand copy is _enrich_like_fetcher in tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_link_removal_2b16.py:103-125 — a verbatim quote of those lines, used by 4 G1 tests. Drift risk is concrete: the copy is not import-linked to production, so a semantic change to the production merge (e.g. writing an empty list for unobserved issues) leaves the copy — and every G1 test — green. (3) The sibling pattern already exists: merge_parent_map (fetcher.py:396, ticket 88d9) was extracted for exactly this reason; the issuelinks helper will mirror it (name: merge_issuelinks_map, same module, mutate-and-return, call site replaces the inline loop). Plan: characterization assertion BEFORE extraction, then extract, delete _enrich_like_fetcher, point tests at the real seam, add key-present/key-absent property test + the mutation check (unobserved issue gaining an empty list must go RED)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785858108818999001,"uuid":"2778c0fa-ea5e-4555-a183-1a922d7cd683"}